Subject: [PATCH] gpio: brcmstb: only abort suspend when a parent IRQ exists

brcmstb_gpio_suspend_noirq() aborts with -EBUSY whenever priv->suspended is
false, to catch a wakeup arriving between ->suspend() and ->suspend_noirq().

But ->suspend() only ever sets that flag when the controller has a parent IRQ:

	static int brcmstb_gpio_suspend(struct device *dev)
	{
		if (priv->parent_irq > 0)
			priv->suspended = true;
		return 0;
	}

A GPIO bank with no parent IRQ therefore can never satisfy the noirq test, and
fails every single suspend with -EBUSY -- not because anything is busy, but
because the flag it checks is never armed. Since the flag is also what the bank
IRQ handler clears to signal "a wake fired mid-suspend", a bank with no parent
IRQ has nothing to catch in the first place.

BCM2712 (Raspberry Pi 5 / CM5) hits this: gpio@7d517c00 has no `interrupts`
property in the device tree, so s2idle aborts 100% of the time with

  brcmstb-gpio 107d517c00.gpio: PM: dpm_run_callback(): brcmstb_gpio_suspend_noirq returns -16
  brcmstb-gpio 107d517c00.gpio: PM: failed to suspend noirq: error -16
  PM: noirq suspend of devices failed

while the sibling bank gpio@7d508500, which does have a parent IRQ, suspends
fine. Make the guard symmetric with the condition that arms it.

--- a/drivers/gpio/gpio-brcmstb.c
+++ b/drivers/gpio/gpio-brcmstb.c
@@ -603,8 +603,15 @@ static int brcmstb_gpio_suspend_noirq(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct brcmstb_gpio_priv *priv = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 
-	/* Catch any wakeup sources occurring between suspend and noirq */
-	if (!priv->suspended)
+	/*
+	 * Catch any wakeup sources occurring between suspend and noirq.
+	 *
+	 * ->suspend() only arms priv->suspended when a parent IRQ exists, and
+	 * only the bank IRQ handler clears it. A controller without a parent
+	 * IRQ has no wake to catch, so testing the flag there would reject
+	 * every suspend with -EBUSY. Keep the guard symmetric with ->suspend().
+	 */
+	if (priv->parent_irq > 0 && !priv->suspended)
 		return -EBUSY;
 
 	if (priv->parent_irq > 0)
